=== each kind of failure is caught, and none of them prints ===
fail -> -999
assert false -> -999
divmod by zero -> -999
pow negative exp -> -999
int_of_str junk -> -999
no failure -> 42
=== a caught failure must not leave the catch armed ===
success after catch -> 7
1 2 3 4
=== work before the failure still happened ===
buffer = onetwothree
=== nesting: the inner catch takes it, the outer sees success ===
5
6
10
=== the value type does not have to be int ===
fallback
true
(0, 0)
=== and a caught failure inside a function that keeps going ===
3 0 0 17
0
